--- c-defects attempt 7, 2026-09-01 ---

D-C16: THE COMMON RUNTIME'S PREFIX-CACHED WARMUP CASE IS BLOCK-ALIGNED, AND GALAXY NEEDS
       CHUNK-ALIGNMENT.

  ValueError: chunk_start must be non-negative and aligned to chunk_alignment
  models/common/modules/attention/attention_2d.py:908

NAMING: attempt 6's handoff section 28 calls this "D-C13". D-C13 is already taken - it is the
superseded global-CB fragmentation OOM recorded in D-C7.status. This defect is D-C16.

MEASURED AT HEAD (671802f9464), three fresh processes, byte-identical, same file and line:
  y1_exec_warmup_df_r1   1 failed  561.12 s   logs/y1_exec_warmup_df_r1.log:2055
  y2_exec_warmup_df_r2   1 failed  219.14 s   logs/y2_exec_warmup_df_r2.log:2055
  y3_exec_warmup_df_r3   1 failed  197.25 s   logs/y3_exec_warmup_df_r3.log:2055
  node: models/common/tests/models/llama33_70b_galaxy/test_executor_wh_galaxy.py
        ::test_executor_warmup_and_program_identity[wormhole_b0-decode_first-...]
  grep -c 'clash with L1 buffers' on all three: 0.

THE MEASURED VALUES, read off y1_exec_warmup_df_r1.log:2038-2040:
  PrefillMetadata(sequence_length=128, user_ids=(0,), chunk_start=32, prefix_user_id=0)
  KVCacheBinding(... PagedKVMetadata(block_size=32, max_num_blocks=2048, ...))
  Galaxy chunk_alignment = 128  (recipes.py:693; and it IS the flash-SDPA q_chunk_size /
  k_chunk_size at recipes.py:651-652, so it is not an arbitrary constant)
  32 % 128 = 32, so the validator refuses.

THE CHAIN, every link verified in the source at HEAD:
  llm_runtime/warmup.py:700        cached_tokens=layout.block_size          <- 32 on Galaxy,
                                   hard-coded inside _build_plan, no config field reaches it
  llm_runtime/prefill/plan.py:163  validates num_cached_tokens % block_size <- the RUNTIME's
                                   own invariant is BLOCK alignment
  llm_runtime/prefill/plan.py:381  absolute_start = num_cached_tokens + relative_start
  llm_runtime/prefill/plan.py:403  chunk_start_idx=absolute_start           <- 32
  modules/attention/attention_2d.py:906  chunk_start % recipe.chunk_alignment

So the common runtime's default warmup plan assumes that any BLOCK-aligned prefix is a valid
chunk start. On Galaxy the block size is 32 and the chunk alignment is 128, and it is not.

WHOSE DEFECT IT IS: the module validator is correct and the shared Galaxy recipe is correct.
The assumption is the runtime's, and the failing line is in llm_runtime. This is a RUNTIME
defect and this brief's prohibition applies without qualification.

WHAT WOULD FIX IT (for whoever owns llm_runtime; do NOT do these in c-defects):
  a) _build_plan asks the model/layout for its chunk alignment rather than assuming the block
     size - the topology-neutral form is a frozen config value on WarmupConfig, defaulting to
     layout.block_size so every existing caller is preserved byte for byte; or
  b) the model-owned executor supplies a warmup plan whose cached_tokens is a multiple of the
     recipe's chunk_alignment. That is c-exec-llama's file, not this job's.

WHAT I DID NOT DO: lowering Galaxy's chunk_alignment from 128 to 32 would make this green and
would be relaxing a constraint to turn a failure green. It is also wrong on the merits -
chunk_alignment IS the flash-SDPA chunk size. Not done.

CONSEQUENCE, and it is narrower than it looks: this fails the PREFIX-CACHED warmup case, not a
plain prefill after a decode. The direct test of whether serving is unblocked -
test_executor_repeated_startup_and_cleanup, three startup/serve/cleanup cycles in one process -
PASSES 3/3 at HEAD (y4/y5/y6, 199.68 / 199.28 / 199.83 s, 0 clash lines each). At 2b463f17fcd
that node failed 3/3 on the L1 address clash. See llama-address-clash.status.
